<article class="env-lemma" id="05AQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05AQ">Lemma <span data-tag="05AQ">31.5.7</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $x \in \text{Supp}(\mathcal{F})$ be a point in the support of $\mathcal{F}$ which is not a specialization of another point of $\text{Supp}(\mathcal{F})$. Then $x \in \text{WeakAss}(\mathcal{F})$. In particular, any generic point of an irreducible component of $X$ is weakly associated to $\mathcal{O}_ X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $x \in \text{Supp}(\mathcal{F})$ the module $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is not zero. Hence $\text{WeakAss}(\mathcal{F}_ x) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{X, x})$ is nonempty by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0588" data-tag="0588">10.66.5</a>. On the other hand, by assumption $\text{Supp}(\mathcal{F}_ x) = \{ \mathfrak m_ x\} $. Since $\text{WeakAss}(\mathcal{F}_ x) \subset \text{Supp}(\mathcal{F}_ x)$ (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0589" data-tag="0589">10.66.6</a>) we see that $\mathfrak m_ x$ is weakly associated to $\mathcal{F}_ x$ and we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>